  "filled_passage": "Our class opened a small stall at the winter fair. The students brought (1) their old toys from home, and the teacher checked that everything was clean. We (2) sold most of the toys during the first hour. A girl who bought a toy rabbit told us she had wanted one for months.\n\nThe afternoon became much (3) colder than the morning. We moved the table away from the open door and wrapped the glass jars (4) carefully so that they would not break. Nobody hurried while doing that job, even when a queue began to form. It was our (5) first fair as a class, so we were still finding out how to organise things.\n\nWe stayed late (6) because the last visitors had only just arrived. Several people had (7) made cards and decorations which they wanted to show us before leaving. The younger (8) children put their cards beside the jars, and their parents helped them write the prices.\n\nAt the end, we had no (9) choice about where to put the money: we had promised it all to the school breakfast project. We counted it with the teacher and waited (10) for her to write the total on the board. The classroom was untidy, but everyone wanted to do the fair again next year.",
